>   Vendor: KONICA    Model: MCD3130SSOMD8130  Rev: 0040
>   Type:   Optical Device                     ANSI SCSI revision: 02
> Detected scsi removable disk sda at scsi0, channel 0, id 6, lun 0
>   Vendor: DEC       Model: RZ2CC-KB (C) DEC  Rev: DC2B
>   Type:   Direct-Access                      ANSI SCSI revision: 02
> Detected scsi disk sdb at scsi1, channel 0, id 0, lun 0
> scsi : detected 2 SCSI disks total.
[..]
> SCSI ID of MO is "6" and its ID of  HDD is "0", but sda is MO and sdb is
> HDD.
> "sda" was HDD when MO was not connected.
> I don' know why MO locates before HDD.
> 
Because it detects the adaptec before the qlogic.
And since the SCSI-drives are numbered consecutively, all drives
connected to the adaptec will be assigned letters before any drive
connected to the qlogic.

Solution: either connect the HD to the adaptec or the MO to the qlogic.
Or live with it as it is. 

> I tried to install again connecting to MO drive.
> Installation began. But the installer indicated
> "/dev/sda - SCSI ID 0 - Model Dec RZ2CC-KB (C) DEC"
> at the window of Partition Disks, and didn't allow me to "edit" HDD and
> "fdisk /tmp/sdb".
> That's funny because I inserted MO media, I can "edit" HDD which is MO
> media and set petitions.
> 
Hmm. Makes sense. How would you expect to set partitions on a MO-drive
with no media in it ??

Remember: The numbering scheme in Linux and AlphaBIOS (which presumably
is what you're using) are to different things, even when they might look
similar.

HTH,

Hannes
